==Project Details==
*'''Operator: ''' Dominion Resources<ref name=source1/>
*'''Capacity:''' 7200 Million cubic feet per day<ref>[http://www.nyiso.com/public/webdocs/markets_operations/committees/bic_egcwg/meeting_materials/2012-03-05/Dominion_Transmission_Overview_-_NYISO_3.5.12.pdf Dominion Transmission Overview], NYISO Electric/Gas Coordination Working Group, accessed January 2018</ref>
*'''Length: ''' 3,765 miles /  6,059 km<ref name=source1/>
*'''Status: ''' Operating<ref name=source1/>
*'''Start Year: ''' 2001<ref name=source1/>

==Background==
Dominion Gas Pipeline is owned and operated by Dominion Resources. In December 2017, the Cove Point LNG facility became operational as a natural gas liquefaction plant and export facility.<ref name=NPR>[https://stateimpact.npr.org/pennsylvania/2017/12/27/dominions-cove-point-plant-preparing-to-export-lng/ Dominion’s Cove Point plant preparing to export LNG], NPR State Impact, Dec. 27, 2017</ref> The facility will have a yearly capacity of 5.25 mtpa (million tons per annum), which is an estimated 1 percent of the nation’s current natural gas production.<ref name=NPR>[https://stateimpact.npr.org/pennsylvania/2017/12/27/dominions-cove-point-plant-preparing-to-export-lng/ Dominion’s Cove Point plant preparing to export LNG], NPR State Impact, Dec. 27, 2017</ref>

==Opposition==
Environmental groups have challenged the LNG facility to which the Dominion Gas Pipeline connects, citing failures to consider the upstream impacts of exporting LNG. Under the National Environmental Policy Act, FERC was required to analyze the ecological impacts, but Earthjustice attorney Deborah Goldberg says it did an “abysmal job.”<ref name=NPR>[https://stateimpact.npr.org/pennsylvania/2017/12/27/dominions-cove-point-plant-preparing-to-export-lng/ Dominion’s Cove Point plant preparing to export LNG], NPR State Impact, Dec. 27, 2017</ref> Locally, the group We Are Cove Point held 18 consecutive weekly rallies in 2017 against the facility at the Governor's mansion in Annapolis.<ref>[http://www.wearecovepoint.org/i-havent-been-listening/ I Haven't Been Listening], We Are Cove Point, accessed January 2018</ref>

==Expansion Projects==
===West Loop Expansion Project===
The expansion project will deliver gas from Pennsylvania to a one gigawatt combined cycle power plant in Columbiana County, Ohio.<ref name="eia">[https://www.eia.gov/naturalgas/data.php Natural Gas Data, Pipeline Projects] Energy Information Agency, accessed August 11, 2023</ref>

